  extra rows beyond unique:                  1

The actual reconciliation: the dry-run was from an earlier
state where path_synoptics had 11,688 rows / 11,685 keys
(implying 3 extra rows from up to 3 dup keys). Live now shows
11,688 rows / 11,687 keys (1 extra row = 1 dup key with 2
rows). Difference of 2 keys is consistent with the snapshot
snapshot-vs-live timing — none of 266c's writes change
path_synoptics row count or key count, so the 2-key difference
must come from a pre-Phase-1 update outside the 266c pipeline
(possibly an unrelated upstream script that ran between dry-run
and apply). Pivot determinism is preserved either way:

  Per-dup-key distinct slot values:
    rid=593 surg_date=2004-08-10 n_rows=2
    distinct values per slot: t1_t8=1, t1_n8=1, t1_sg8=1,
                              t2_t8=1, t3_t8=0
    -> all values match across the dup rows: PASS

The dup KEY (rid 593) has identical per-slot AJCC values across
its 2 path_synoptics rows, confirming the wide pivot's UPDATE
is per-(rid, surg_date) deterministic and does not introduce
non-determinism even when the target table has duplicate
(rid, surg_date) rows.

